// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6094 Add Sysinternals tooling and driver/UAC detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6094
// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading Via AccCheckConsole.EXE
// Sigma ID: c2b3a9c9-0a66-4e8a-aea2-a4c4f95dd933
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1574.001, T1127
// Description: Detects "AccCheckConsole.exe" (UI Accessibility Checker, a signed Microsoft binary) loading a
//   DLL from a user-writable / non-system location. The utility accepts a user-supplied DLL
//   containing a custom verification routine, which is then loaded into the trusted process context.
//   Adversaries abuse this to proxy execution of an attacker-controlled DLL and bypass application
//   whitelisting.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the UI Accessibility Checker with verification routine DLLs stored in user directories
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/AccCheckConsole/
//   - https://gist.github.com/bohops/2444129419c8acf837aedda5f0e7f340
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_lolbin_acccheckconsole_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\AccCheckConsole.exe" and FolderPath endswith ".dll") and (not((FolderPath contains "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Program Files\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\")))
